From fc8f0090ee4fb4d29d217192360b54acf48f3c37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:00:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Kanban sync: the owner's repair never sends a card
 back to running over its ended run

Hub 2026-11-12 08:27:50Z: worker-4 completed the hub's t_01a1ceaeb6ba593c (Board v18-v20: done, run
done/completed, current_run_uid NULL). The hub's live row still held the v16 task fields at the replica's
version 20. repair_divergence read "equal version, fields differ" as an uncaptured local write and queued
status=running, completed_at=NULL, the ended run as current_run_uid and the old block_kind /
completion_contract (base_version 20). The Board merges task fields per field by HLC, so the hub's newer
clock won every field: v21. In the same pass t_01a1ceb44e35f780 (todo after a blocked run on worker-5) became
v11 running. Both then read running with no claim, no lease and an ended run in every copy, and nothing sweeps
that shape (the stale-claim sweep needs a claim to expire).

- repair_divergence: when the live status differs and the live current run has already ended (or the
  replica is done/archived on the same run), the live copy is the stale one. Apply the replica's row to live
  (feed apply, nothing captured or sent) instead of re-sending live's.
- heal_running_over_ended_run (primary rounds, next to heal_clobbered_completions): a card that reads running
  with no claim_lock, no lease and an ended current run goes to done when that run ended completed and the
  latest completed event names it, else to todo (the promoter makes it ready once parents are done). The write
  goes through the capture triggers, so the Board is corrected by the same round's push. It runs once per run:
  a heal the Board outvotes is logged and left alone, so it never loops.

Tests: test_kanban_sync_terminal_regress.py reproduces the regressing write (RED on main: both parametrized
cases queue status/current_run_uid/completion_contract, Board ends at running). test_kanban_sync_running_heal.py
covers the already-regressed shape, the once-per-run bound and an open run left alone.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_sync_client.py              |   2 +
 hermes_cli/kanban_sync_divergence.py          |  87 ++++++++++
 .../test_kanban_sync_running_heal.py          |  78 +++++++++
 .../test_kanban_sync_terminal_regress.py      | 151 ++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 318 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_running_heal.py
 create mode 100644 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_terminal_regress.py

